# `range` is not a name the compiler knows. The counting form
# `for i in range(a, b, step):` and the `range` builtin were deleted on
# 2026-07-29 (the loops-cleanup plan); the three-clause `for` replaces it, and
# `parallel for i in 0..<N:` replaces it inside a `parallel for`.
#
# `range` was never a procedure -- it was recognised only by lexeme inside a
# `for` header (src/tychoc.c:3387), so its removal is the removal of that one
# branch. This fixture asserts the header form is refused. `x := range(3)` has
# always said "unknown procedure 'range'" and still does.
#
# This lane (tests/run.sh:170-185) asserts only a nonzero exit and a non-empty
# diagnostic. The exact message -- which must name the three-clause form as the
# replacement -- is locked byte-for-byte by tests/diag/range_removed.err.
#
# Replaces three range()-only fixtures deleted by phase 6's sweep:
# tests/reject/range_step_zero_lit.ty, tests/abort/range_step_zero.ty and
# tests/conc/reject/parfor_step.ty. None was restorable: all three asserted
# properties of `range()`'s step argument, and no step argument exists in
# either replacement form.

fn main():
    for i in range(3):
        println(str(i))
